486
00:32:46.465 --> 00:32:47.590
Take her to the zoo.

487
00:32:47.716 --> 00:32:49.592
Come on out of the car!

488
00:32:56.099 --> 00:32:59.393
-Some more coffee. Mr. Creed?
-No. thanks. Shirley.

489
00:33:00.062 --> 00:33:01.896
What do you think about Billy Snow?

490
00:33:01.938 --> 00:33:03.105
Fouls.

491
00:33:04.608 --> 00:33:06.484
How about Big Chuck Smith?

492
00:33:06.568 --> 00:33:08.611
No. he's too old and dull.

493
00:33:08.779 --> 00:33:10.738
Hey. that Bobby Judge. he's a good boy.

494
00:33:10.781 --> 00:33:12.490
No. I don't feel no heat from that name.

495
00:33:12.574 --> 00:33:14.742
Joe Zack's a good prospect.

496
00:33:15.952 --> 00:33:18.788
Exactly what are you looking for. Apollo?

497
00:33:19.915 --> 00:33:22.124
This is what I'm looking for.

498
00:33:22.292 --> 00:33:24.418
The Italian Stallion.

499
00:33:24.795 --> 00:33:27.254
Rocky Balboa? Never heard of him.

500
00:33:27.673 --> 00:33:29.757
Look. it's the name. man.

501
00:33:29.800 --> 00:33:31.801
The Italian Stallion.

502
00:33:32.761 --> 00:33:34.428
The media will eat it up.

503
00:33:34.471 --> 00:33:37.306
Who discovered America?
An Italian. right?

504
00:33:37.641 --> 00:33:41.143
What would be better than to get it on
with one of his descendants?

505
00:33:41.269 --> 00:33:42.687
He's a southpaw.

506
00:33:42.771 --> 00:33:44.480
I don't want you messing around
with southpaws.

507
00:33:44.606 --> 00:33:46.649
-They do everything backwards.
-Southpaw nothing.

508
00:33:46.775 --> 00:33:48.651
I'll drop him in three.

509
00:33:49.778 --> 00:33:53.489
Apollo Creed meets the Italian Stallion.

510
00:33:55.283 --> 00:33:57.368
Sounds like a damn monster movie.

511
00:33:57.703 --> 00:33:59.787
What are you doing with that bat?

512
00:33:59.830 --> 00:34:01.497
I used to be deadly at stickball.

513
00:34:01.623 --> 00:34:04.458
-Your sister knows I'm coming?
-PAULIE: She's very excited.

514
00:34:04.793 --> 00:34:06.877
-Look at these swollen hands.
-Yeah.

515
00:34:06.962 --> 00:34:10.381
The joints from carrying meat
in and out of the freezer.

516
00:34:10.465 --> 00:34:13.676
-Plays hell on the joints.
-Maybe you ought to see a doctor.

517
00:34:13.802 --> 00:34:15.678
I don't need a doctor.
I need a different job.

518
00:34:15.804 --> 00:34:18.180
Different job. What kind of turkey?
Big? Small?

519
00:34:18.306 --> 00:34:21.642
Talk to Gazzo. Tell him I'm a good man.

520
00:34:21.727 --> 00:34:24.812
Nothing bothers me.
I'd make a great collector.

521
00:34:24.855 --> 00:34:26.856
Busting bones don't bother me.

522
00:34:26.982 --> 00:34:29.316
Don't bother you. Big turkey. right?

523
00:34:29.401 --> 00:34:32.403
Gazzo's gotta give me. . . Forget Gazzo.
It's a bad job.

524
00:34:32.487 --> 00:34:34.029
You got a match?

525
00:34:34.156 --> 00:34:36.031
Go to him for me. As a favor.

526
00:34:36.158 --> 00:34:38.868
Yeah. yeah. Last time I had a turkey

527
00:34:38.994 --> 00:34:42.496
was when they had a two-dollar special
at Horn and Hardart's three years ago.

528
00:34:42.539 --> 00:34:45.040
Last year. me and the turtles had Spam.

529
00:34:45.375 --> 00:34:46.751
(ALL CHATTERING)

530
00:34:53.341 --> 00:34:57.219
-Your sister knows I'm coming?
-Yeah. yeah. She's very excited.

531
00:34:58.889 --> 00:35:00.514
(SlNGlNG) l'm all alone

532
00:35:00.599 --> 00:35:03.017
Will you forget about Gazzo?

533
00:35:03.685 --> 00:35:05.186
I don't ask nobody twice.

534
00:35:05.228 --> 00:35:07.188
Don't ask nobody twice.

535
00:35:07.355 --> 00:35:09.690
(SlNGlNG) Stay away. baby

536
00:35:09.900 --> 00:35:11.192
(DOG BARKING)

537
00:35:12.694 --> 00:35:14.612
You're sure your sister knows I'm coming?

538
00:35:14.696 --> 00:35:16.739
Yeah. She's very excited.

539
00:35:20.410 --> 00:35:22.203
ADRIAN: Paulie. you're late.

540
00:35:23.205 --> 00:35:24.538
You call the hospital?

541
00:35:24.581 --> 00:35:27.708
She calls the hospital
if I'm ten minutes late.

542
00:35:28.585 --> 00:35:30.294
ROCKY: Yo. how you doing?

543
00:35:31.379 --> 00:35:33.756
I told you. she's very excited.

544
00:35:36.384 --> 00:35:38.719
ADRIAN: Why didn't you tell me
you were bringing him here?

545
00:35:38.762 --> 00:35:40.387
I'm not ready for this.

546
00:35:40.430 --> 00:35:42.890
PAULIE: Would it make a difference
if you were?

547
00:35:42.933 --> 00:35:45.392
-He's taking you out.
-No. I can't.

548
00:35:46.728 --> 00:35:49.438
PAULIE: I want you out of the kitchen
right now.

549
00:35:50.106 --> 00:35:51.398
I won't.

550
00:35:56.238 --> 00:35:58.781
I want you out of here instamatically!

551
00:35:58.907 --> 00:36:01.492
I'm sick of seeing you
hanging around like a freaking spider.

552
00:36:01.576 --> 00:36:03.744
Go out and live. Enjoy life!

553
00:36:03.954 --> 00:36:05.579
ADRIAN: I can't go!

554
00:36:05.664 --> 00:36:07.581
Don't get wise with me now.

555
00:36:07.666 --> 00:36:09.416
I'm tired of you being a loser.

556
00:36:09.459 --> 00:36:11.627
Don't call me that. Paulie!

557
00:36:11.753 --> 00:36:14.630
ANNOUNCER ON TV: Apollo Creed says
he'll be shopping for another victim

558
00:36:14.756 --> 00:36:18.467
to fill Green's vacancy
for the Bicentennial championship fight...

559
00:36:18.593 --> 00:36:20.261
Why didn't you tell me
you were bringing him home?

560
00:36:20.345 --> 00:36:21.637
How do you know I didn't?

561
00:36:21.763 --> 00:36:24.598
I can't go. Paulie. I won't go!

562
00:36:24.641 --> 00:36:25.766
Why?

563
00:36:26.768 --> 00:36:30.187
Paulie. it's Thanksgiving.
I got a turkey in the oven.

564
00:36:30.939 --> 00:36:32.940
Oh. a turkey in the oven.

565
00:36:39.656 --> 00:36:41.448
Turkey in the oven.

566
00:36:48.498 --> 00:36:52.209
You want the bird?
Go in the alley and eat the bird !

567
00:36:52.836 --> 00:36:54.295
Aw. Paulie!

568
00:36:55.297 --> 00:36:58.299
I want you out of here!
Get out of the house!

569
00:36:58.508 --> 00:37:01.051
Go out and enjoy your freaking life!

570
00:37:01.177 --> 00:37:02.344
(ADRIAN YELLING)

571
00:37:05.307 --> 00:37:06.974
You hungry. Rock?

572
00:37:13.648 --> 00:37:17.318
Hey. yo. Paulie. maybe we better
forget all this. you know?

573
00:37:17.819 --> 00:37:20.988
Forget nothing. Go ahead.
Tell her something funny.

574
00:37:21.031 --> 00:37:24.199
Ain't nothing to talk about.
She's in a bad mood. I'm in a bad mood.

575
00:37:24.326 --> 00:37:27.036
You can do funny things.
You wanna go out with my sister?

576
00:37:27.162 --> 00:37:28.662
-Yeah.
-Well. . .

577
00:37:32.876 --> 00:37:34.501
I don't know what to say.

578
00:37:34.586 --> 00:37:35.753
Funny.

579
00:37:47.390 --> 00:37:49.516
Yo. Adrian. It's me. Rocky.

580
00:37:49.893 --> 00:37:51.560
Rocky. you know?

581
00:37:52.228 --> 00:37:53.437
Listen.

582
00:37:55.732 --> 00:38:00.194
I don't know what to say. 'cause I ain't
never talked to no door before.

583
00:38:01.363 --> 00:38:04.573
What do I say to a door?
We better forget this.

584
00:38:04.866 --> 00:38:06.075
You're doing fine.

585
00:38:06.201 --> 00:38:08.535
I ain't doing fine. I look like an idiot.

586
00:38:08.578 --> 00:38:10.579
Keep doing what you're doing. Funny.

587
00:38:10.705 --> 00:38:12.873
I know all about these things.

588
00:38:12.958 --> 00:38:14.708
I feel like a jerk.

589
00:38:20.715 --> 00:38:23.133
Yo. Adrian. it's Rocky again.

590
00:38:23.218 --> 00:38:27.805
Listen. I know you ain't too happy
at this moment.

591
00:38:28.390 --> 00:38:30.057
But could you do me a favor?

592
00:38:30.100 --> 00:38:33.102
I ain't got nobody
to spend Thanksgiving with.

593
00:38:33.269 --> 00:38:36.605
So. how about maybe you and I

594
00:38:36.731 --> 00:38:38.482
go out together. get something to eat.

595
00:38:38.566 --> 00:38:41.110
Maybe laugh a little bit.
Who knows. you know?

596
00:38:41.236 --> 00:38:42.945
Would you like to. . .

597
00:38:44.781 --> 00:38:47.616
Would you like to. maybe.
you and me go out together?

598
00:38:47.742 --> 00:38:50.285
What do you think? Would you like to?

599
00:38:55.291 --> 00:38:57.501
We're gonna have a good time.

600
00:38:57.919 --> 00:39:00.087
We'll have a real good time.

601
00:39:04.592 --> 00:39:06.427
Thanks for the bird.

602
00:39:10.015 --> 00:39:12.933
I'm gonna turn the TV off.
I got a headache.

603
00:39:25.280 --> 00:39:27.698
-What's your sister like to do?
-Ice-skate.

604
00:39:27.782 --> 00:39:29.783
Adrian. come on.
You're letting the heat out.

605
00:39:29.868 --> 00:39:32.161
Who pays the bills around here?

606
00:39:37.792 --> 00:39:40.878
Listen. I don't want no turkey anyway.
you know?

607
00:39:42.464 --> 00:39:44.465
But it was Thanksgiving.

608
00:39:45.300 --> 00:39:46.467
What?

609
00:39:46.509 --> 00:39:48.469
-It was Thanksgiving.
-Yeah. to you.

610
00:39:48.553 --> 00:39:50.846
But to me it's Thursday. right?

611
00:40:15.205 --> 00:40:17.873
-It looks kind of quiet.
-I think it's closed.

612
00:40:17.999 --> 00:40:21.085
No. I think we're just early
or something like that.

613
00:40:22.504 --> 00:40:24.338
-We're closed.
-What?

614
00:40:24.672 --> 00:40:27.674
-I said we're closed.
-Yeah. Hey. listen.

615
00:40:27.717 --> 00:40:31.053
I'm gonna smooth this guy out. Wait here.
I'll be right back.

616
00:40:31.262 --> 00:40:33.055
-We could go someplace else.
-No. it's okay.

617
00:40:33.181 --> 00:40:37.101
Are you closed to the general public.
or are you just closed to everybody?

618
00:40:37.185 --> 00:40:41.355
It's after 6:00. It's Thanksgiving.
That's why there's nobody here.

619
00:40:41.689 --> 00:40:43.732
Besides. you ain't supposed to be in here.

620
00:40:43.858 --> 00:40:46.360
So do me a favor and not stay here.

621
00:40:46.402 --> 00:40:49.947
-Could you do me a favor?
-Come on. We're not operating.

622
00:40:50.198 --> 00:40:53.033
Look. This girl here ain't feeling well.

623
00:40:53.118 --> 00:40:55.702
Doctors say she should go out
and exercise.

624
00:40:55.745 --> 00:40:57.871
Ice-skating's probably the best thing.

625
00:40:57.956 --> 00:40:59.206
So what do you want from me?

626
00:40:59.290 --> 00:41:01.208
Well. hey. I want you to do me a favor.

627
00:41:01.251 --> 00:41:02.876
You can see she ain't feeling too good.

628
00:41:02.919 --> 00:41:05.921
If you can let her on the ice
for a few minutes. I'd appreciate it.

629
00:41:06.047 --> 00:41:07.798
Ten minutes. ten bucks.

630
00:41:07.882 --> 00:41:10.050
Ten bucks? How about eight bucks?

631
00:41:10.135 --> 00:41:12.261
Come on. It's Thanksgiving.

632
00:41:12.554 --> 00:41:14.388
All right. Nine bucks. you got a deal.

633
00:41:14.472 --> 00:41:17.224
You have the ice to yourself. Ten bucks.

634
00:41:19.394 --> 00:41:21.103
Give her the blades.

635
00:41:21.896 --> 00:41:23.230
Aren't you skating?

636
00:41:23.273 --> 00:41:25.232
No. I ain't skated since I was 1 5.

637
00:41:25.316 --> 00:41:27.609
That's when I started fighting.

638
00:41:27.902 --> 00:41:30.571
Skating's kind of bad for the ankles.
you know?

639
00:41:31.573 --> 00:41:34.283
You're a pretty good skater. aren't you?

640
00:41:35.076 --> 00:41:37.578
Like I was saying
before on the way over here.

641
00:41:37.662 --> 00:41:40.831
fighting used to be tops with me.
but no more.

642
00:41:40.915 --> 00:41:43.417
All I wanted to do out of fighting
was prove I was no bum.

643
00:41:43.501 --> 00:41:45.919
that I had the stuff to make a good pro.

644
00:41:46.004 --> 00:41:49.006
-You never got the chance?
-I ain't crying about it.

645
00:41:49.090 --> 00:41:51.341
I still fight. I do it like a hobby.

646
00:41:51.426 --> 00:41:53.594
The trouble is I'm a southpaw.

647
00:41:53.678 --> 00:41:56.597
-What's a southpaw?
-A southpaw means you're left-handed.

648
00:41:56.681 --> 00:41:59.057
A southpaw throws your timing off.

649
00:41:59.142 --> 00:42:01.435
It throws other guys' timing off.
makes them look awkward.

650
00:42:01.519 --> 00:42:03.103
Nobody wants to look awkward.

651
00:42:03.188 --> 00:42:06.356
-You know where "southpaw" came from?
-MAN: Nine minutes!

652
00:42:06.441 --> 00:42:09.484
A long time ago. there was this guy.
maybe a couple hundred years ago.

653
00:42:09.569 --> 00:42:13.030
he was fighting in the. . .
I think it was around Philadelphia.

654
00:42:13.114 --> 00:42:17.075
His arm. . . He was left-handed.
His arm was facing towards New Jersey.

655
00:42:17.160 --> 00:42:20.996
And that's south. So naturally
they called him "south paw." You see?

656
00:42:21.080 --> 00:42:24.374
Southpaw. South Jersey. South Camden.

657
00:42:24.834 --> 00:42:26.668
Southpaw. You know what I mean?

658
00:42:28.171 --> 00:42:30.297
Things probably worked out for the best.
don't you think?

659
00:42:30.381 --> 00:42:33.050
Never got a chance
because you're left-handed. huh?

660
00:42:33.134 --> 00:42:35.219
That's absolutely true. you know?

661
00:42:35.303 --> 00:42:36.553
Watch out.

662
00:42:37.055 --> 00:42:38.472
(GROANING)

663
00:42:38.556 --> 00:42:41.600
Ah ! Ah ! I just dislocated my finger.

664
00:42:41.935 --> 00:42:43.477
Ah ! Look at that.

665
00:42:44.229 --> 00:42:46.021
Wait. It ain't your fault. Look.

666
00:42:46.105 --> 00:42:48.482
See? I had it. . . It's an old wound.

667
00:42:48.566 --> 00:42:50.817
You see that? Look. See?

668
00:42:50.902 --> 00:42:52.319
Nothing. It bends like that.

669
00:42:52.403 --> 00:42:55.364
I originally done it. . . Push the button.
Bong. It works.

670
00:42:55.448 --> 00:42:58.325
-It ain't your fault. Look.
-MAN: Seven minutes!

671
00:42:59.077 --> 00:43:02.079
I originally done it. . .
I carry pictures of all my fights.

672
00:43:02.163 --> 00:43:04.915
I originally done it
in the Baby Crenshaw fight.

673
00:43:04.999 --> 00:43:08.043
ROCKY: Baby's about the size of an
airplane. I broke both hands on his face.

674
00:43:08.127 --> 00:43:11.505
I lost that fight. but that's a nice picture.
don't you think?

675
00:43:11.589 --> 00:43:12.923
Real nice.

676
00:43:14.384 --> 00:43:16.760
Come on. You having a good time?

677
00:43:17.470 --> 00:43:19.388
You can see I ain't too graceful.

678
00:43:19.472 --> 00:43:23.850
I don't move well. but I can really swat.
I can really hit hard.

679
00:43:23.935 --> 00:43:27.604
But I'm a southpaw.
and nobody wants to fight no southpaw.

680
00:43:31.317 --> 00:43:32.734
(WHOOPS)

681
00:43:32.819 --> 00:43:35.570
You know how I got started in fighting?

682
00:43:35.655 --> 00:43:36.780
No.

683
00:43:37.532 --> 00:43:39.449
Am I talking too loud?

684
00:43:39.742 --> 00:43:41.326
MAN: Three minutes!

685
00:43:41.411 --> 00:43:45.956
My father. he's a. . .
My old man. he was never too smart.

686
00:43:46.040 --> 00:43:48.125
He says to me.
"You weren't born with much of a brain.

687
00:43:48.209 --> 00:43:50.711
"so you better start using your body."

688
00:43:50.795 --> 00:43:52.713
So I become a fighter.

689
00:43:53.381 --> 00:43:55.132
You know what I mean?

690
00:43:55.216 --> 00:43:57.050
Why you laughing?

691
00:43:58.386 --> 00:44:01.305
My mother. she said the opposite thing.

692
00:44:01.389 --> 00:44:03.640
What did she say the opposite?

693
00:44:04.267 --> 00:44:06.560
She said.
"You weren't born with much of a body.

694
00:44:06.644 --> 00:44:08.395
"so you better develop your brain."

695
00:44:08.479 --> 00:44:11.231
-Did she say that?
-Yo. time!

696
00:44:12.525 --> 00:44:15.402
-Can I ask you a question?
-Absolutely.

697
00:44:16.654 --> 00:44:20.073
-Why do you wanna fight?
-'Cause I can't sing or dance.

698
00:44:20.158 --> 00:44:21.241
Hey. yo.

699
00:44:21.743 --> 00:44:23.452
ROCKY: Don't fall !

700
00:44:24.704 --> 00:44:27.122
That was terrific. I'm pretty good at this.

701
00:44:27.206 --> 00:44:28.457
You like the way I skate?

702
00:44:28.541 --> 00:44:31.585
Last fight I had.
I had with this guy named Spider Rico.

703
00:44:31.669 --> 00:44:34.379
He busted my head up there.
You see that scar?

704
00:44:34.464 --> 00:44:37.466
I'll tell you.
things get pretty rough in the ring.

705
00:44:46.934 --> 00:44:49.895
You know.
some people are very shy by nature.

706
00:44:50.813 --> 00:44:52.189
I suppose.

707
00:44:53.066 --> 00:44:54.149
(CLEARS THROAT)

708
00:44:55.109 --> 00:44:57.986
I say you're very shy by nature. you know?

709
00:44:59.238 --> 00:45:00.614
I suppose.

710
00:45:03.284 --> 00:45:05.035
The bum from the dark.

711
00:45:05.119 --> 00:45:06.787
Get a job. you bum !

712
00:45:07.622 --> 00:45:10.499
Some people think
that being shy is a disease.

713
00:45:10.583 --> 00:45:12.542
but it don't bother me none.

714
00:45:12.627 --> 00:45:14.544
Don't bother me either.

715
00:45:15.880 --> 00:45:18.006
So why'd I bother bringing it up?

716
00:45:18.091 --> 00:45:20.258
'Cause I'm dumb. that's why.

717
00:45:21.511 --> 00:45:23.553
I think we make
a sharp couple of coconuts.

718
00:45:23.638 --> 00:45:26.473
I'm dumb and you're shy.
What do you think?

719
00:45:28.726 --> 00:45:32.312
I don't understand
why anybody would wanna be a fighter.

720
00:45:32.647 --> 00:45:37.943
You gotta be a moron to wanna
be a fighter. you know what I mean?

721
00:45:38.486 --> 00:45:41.988
It's a racket where you're
almost guaranteed to end up a bum.

722
00:45:42.073 --> 00:45:45.492
-I don't think you're a bum.
-I'm at least half a bum.

723
00:45:45.701 --> 00:45:47.869
But I'll tell you something.

724
00:45:48.746 --> 00:45:51.331
Worst thing about fighting
is the morning after.

725
00:45:51.416 --> 00:45:52.791
-You know?
-Morning after.

726
00:45:52.875 --> 00:45:54.751
Yeah. the morning after a fight.

727
00:45:54.836 --> 00:45:57.379
you're like a large wound.
you know what I mean?

728
00:45:57.463 --> 00:45:59.506
Sometimes I got pains all over me.

729
00:45:59.590 --> 00:46:03.301
I feel like calling a taxi to take me
from the bed into the bathroom.

730
00:46:03.386 --> 00:46:05.262
Your hair hurts. your eyes hurt.

731
00:46:05.346 --> 00:46:08.223
Your face is busted up.
Your hands are swollen.

732
00:46:08.307 --> 00:46:11.393
Look at this face. Sixty-four fights.
Look at that nose.

733
00:46:11.477 --> 00:46:14.229
You see that nose?
That nose ain't never been broken.

734
00:46:14.313 --> 00:46:16.648
I had guys busting on it.

735
00:46:16.732 --> 00:46:19.776
I had guys chewing on it.
twisting and punching it.

736
00:46:19.861 --> 00:46:21.445
I mean. whack. boom.

737
00:46:21.529 --> 00:46:24.030
These guys are hitting my nose
all the time.

738
00:46:24.115 --> 00:46:26.074
Never broke it. I'm very proud of that.

739
00:46:26.159 --> 00:46:27.742
That's rare.

740
00:46:27.827 --> 00:46:30.871
-Why do you do it if it hurts?
-Why you think?

741
00:46:32.290 --> 00:46:34.916
'Cause you can't sing and dance?

742
00:46:35.209 --> 00:46:37.711
Yeah. something like that.

743
00:46:37.795 --> 00:46:39.921
Hey. you wanna come inside?

744
00:46:42.258 --> 00:46:43.508
No. I gotta go.

745
00:46:43.593 --> 00:46:45.552
Hey. come on. I got some animals.

746
00:46:45.636 --> 00:46:48.054
